%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 4b3f2a8c8f344355b16a4d4296ae3f98, type: 3}
  m_Name: Swordfish
  m_EditorClassIdentifier:
  vesselClass: 30
  entries:
  - Element: 1
    AbilityLabel: 'Energize'
    AbilityDescription: 'Hold both triggers to light the blade: it costs nothing and its cooldown is its only limit (the sword has had no energy meter since 2026-10-26). A lit blade lays the afterimages (Mass) and, with the Space level-5 upgrade, pops super-shielded prisms. Charge also scales how many petals a sword hit takes from a rival vessel - x1 at rest (the price Broadside puts on a Strike), x2.5 at level 10, floored at x1 (SwordfishSwordStealBySkimmerEffect.stealScale, read at the thief''s replicated level). Below Charge 5 those petals are knocked loose as crystals at the strike; the level-5 upgrade makes the sword pocket them.'
    Input: 13
    UnlockLevel: 5
    RelockBelowLevel: 4
    LatchPolicy: 0
    UpgradeLabel: 'Sword Steal'
    UpgradeDescription: 'A sword hit on a rival vessel STEALS its petals - they land on the Swordfish instead of being knocked loose as crystals at the strike (the same verb and numbers as the Squirrel''s joust). SwordfishSwordStealBySkimmerEffect.stealUpgradeElement, gated on IsUpgradeActive(Charge) in VesselOvertakeBySkimmerEffectSO.TakeFrom (Garrett, 2026-10-26).'
  - Element: 2
    AbilityLabel: 'Afterimage'
    AbilityDescription: 'When the energized blade goes out, the sword keeps leaving copies of itself - prisms in the blade''s own shape and pose - for 5 s (SwordfishSwordAfterimage, SwordfishSwordAfterimageConfig). The omni-crystal Surge (the crystal is absorbed into the hull; 8 s, a ring of eight trigger-driven swords round it) lays them for its whole length, from the pilot''s blade. Mass scales their VOLUME: x1 at rest, x2.5 at level 10, floored at x0.25, read at the replicated level so every peer lays the same mass. They are not immune to the Swordfish''s own blade: past the 1 s self-trail grace it cuts them like any prism.'
    Input: 13
    UnlockLevel: 5
    RelockBelowLevel: 4
    LatchPolicy: 0
    UpgradeLabel: 'Danger Afterimages'
    UpgradeDescription: 'The afterimages are laid as DANGER prisms (SwordfishSwordAfterimageConfigSO.dangerUpgradeElement, gated on IsUpgradeActive(Mass), snapshotted per afterimage).'
  - Element: 3
    AbilityLabel: 'Blade Reach'
    AbilityDescription: 'Space alone grows the sword: the blade runs 24 at rest to 40 at level 10 (Skimmer.Scale on the Swordfish''s ForceFieldSkimmer, eased in by ShieldSkimmerScaleDriver), and nothing else resizes it - no energy, no surge burst (2026-10-26). The local pilot''s camera pulls back with it, in proportion (ShieldSkimmerScaleConfig.cameraFollowsBladeLength), so the blade reads the same size on screen. Reach is what the blade cuts, what it strikes an Astro League ball with at the tip, and how far the afterimages and the surge''s sword ring reach.'
    Input: 13
    UnlockLevel: 5
    RelockBelowLevel: 4
    LatchPolicy: 0
    UpgradeLabel: 'Shield Breaker'
    UpgradeDescription: 'The sword can destroy SUPER-SHIELDED prisms: an energized blade pops them. Without the upgrade the blade binds in hardened mass, energized or not. ShieldSkimmerScaleConfigSO.superShieldUpgradeElement, gated on IsUpgradeActive(Space) (Garrett, 2026-10-26).'
  - Element: 4
    AbilityLabel: 'Quickdraw'
    AbilityDescription: 'Time is the sword''s RATE: it divides the energize hold (1 s at rest, 0.4 s at level 10), the energize cooldown (5 s -> 2 s) and each swipe''s recovery (0.35 s -> 0.14 s), x1 at rest, x2.5 at level 10, floored at x0.5 (ShieldSkimmerScaleConfig.timeSwordRateMultiplier, SwordfishShieldSwipeConfig.timeSwipeRateMultiplier, read live). The let-go tail stays 5 s. The Swordfish''s own Time card since 2026-11-12, replacing the Ramp Spool it shared with the Rhino: its ramp still winds it to 840 u/s (SwordfishRampBoostAction), but no element scales the wind-up.'
    Input: 13
    UnlockLevel: 5
    RelockBelowLevel: 4
    LatchPolicy: 0
    UpgradeLabel: 'Flurry'
    UpgradeDescription: 'The swipe recovery is gone for good: the sword swings as freely as an energized blade, lit or not (SwordfishShieldSwipeConfigSO.flurryUpgradeElement, gated on IsUpgradeActive(Time) in ShieldSwipeActionExecutor.ApplySwipeRecovery). Replaces Momentum, which stays the Rhino''s.'
  omniAbilityLabel: Surge
